# Pair 4 — Three-Week Moving Average

### Research Question

**Can smoothing the weekly case counts make the overall trend easier to see?**

### Branch

```text
feature/moving-average
```

### File

```text
analysis/pair4_moving_average.R
```

### Tasks

1. Load `malaria_data.csv`.
2. Calculate a three-week moving average of malaria cases.
3. Add the moving average as a new column.
4. Plot the original weekly cases.
5. Add the moving average to the same plot.
6. Include appropriate labels and a title.
7. Add a short comment describing what the smoothed trend shows.

### Starting point

```r
data <- read.csv("malaria_data.csv")

data$moving_avg <- as.numeric(
  stats::filter(
    data$malaria_cases,
    rep(1/3, 3),
    sides = 1
  )
)

# Continue the analysis here
```

### Commit message

```bash
git commit -m "Add three-week moving average analysis"
```

